  scope_statement: >-
    EXP-SYC-b11b38 is an immutable zero-run static design snapshot. Fresh
    independent Validator and Red Team reviews in distinct verified
    review-adversarial xhigh sessions both returned REVISE. They confirm real
    scoped repairs to HA-2 mean calibration, the bits=27 literal, deferred
    finding notation, and peak-axis disclosure, while independently preserving
    three implementation-blocking residual classes: no finite simultaneous
    occupancy-tail certificate for capacity 32; no analytic or measured
    eight-way BSGS peak_live_bytes bound; and archive, communication, and
    output totals over unchanged caps by 3256009664, 3285369792, and 7132160
    bytes. This evidence supports withholding implementation and execution. It
    is not evidence for or against H-SYC-b854f4, ECDLP hardness, an attack, a
    speedup, or a cryptographic-scale claim.
  observations:
    - >-
      Snapshot commit 2ca69be4f08c348ecc4a922e5ec18c1b0a3fa218 has exact
      parent 9ad0c3b74708cf6bd21c852ff052de1a5bb2994b and the seven
      dispatcher-bound paths and hashes. Both reviews independently verified
      that archive boundary.
    - >-
      Validator TASK-20260811-6b1bfb returned REVISE. It confirms that the
      peak-disclosure, bits=27 literal, and deferred-status notation defects
      close at the zero-run specification boundary. It finds candidate_index
      capacity adequacy open because no per-tuple or simultaneous-tail bound
      exists, and it independently reproduces every positive byte-cap residual.
    - >-
      Red Team TASK-20260811-d42301 returned REVISE. At gamma_x=1/3 it gives
      two laws with the same HA-2 mean: X=1 always, and X=33B for a shared
      Bernoulli B with probability 1/33. The latter overflows capacity 32 with
      probability 1/33. This proves a mean alone does not identify capacity
      adequacy. The Red Team also keeps the eight-way peak axis open and
      independently reproduces the three byte-cap residuals.
    - >-
      Zero experiments ran. Both reports and both exact-session receipts bind
      implementation_authorized=false, execution_authorized=false, no fallback,
      no degradation, provider openai, model gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh effort, and
      independently distinct session identifiers. No prohibited provider was
      selected or contacted.
  inference: >-
    Preserve EXP-SYC-b11b38 at review_required and withhold implementation and
    execution. Revisit only through a fresh frozen batch that supplies the
    missing finite simultaneous-tail or propagated-capacity argument, the
    eight-way peak bound/census contract, and an honest capacity-fit decision.
    The current campaign may rerank other committed frontier work while this
    lineage remains parked under those explicit revisit conditions.
  boundaries:
    - No experiment, run, implementation, curve, target, scalar recovery, solver, or benchmark exists under EXP-SYC-b11b38.
    - No attack, speedup, security impact, asymptotic result, cryptographic-scale result, closure result, or breakthrough is supported.
    - HA-2 remains a heuristic; the zero-o(1) arithmetic fixture is not a finite-N theorem or tail model.
    - The cap residuals are apparatus and budget-adequacy findings, not negative evidence against a mathematical hypothesis.
    - GOAL-ECDLP-001 and RQ-ECDLP-002 remain active; H-SYC-b854f4 remains specified without evidential promotion.
  unresolved_confounds:
    - The finite distribution and dependence structure of candidate_index occupancy across 98304 accounting tuples is unspecified.
    - No complete process-wide eight-way BSGS peak_live_bytes observation or analytic upper bound exists.
    - The inherited archive, communication, and output caps are incompatible with the current declared static package absent scope or budget authority.
